{%- style -%}
  .vellano-research {
    background: #F8F6F3;
    color: #111;
    font-family: 'Jost', sans-serif;
    padding: 80px 5% 120px;
  }
  .vellano-research-header {
    text-align: center;
    max-width: 800px;
    margin: 0 auto 80px;
  }
  .vellano-research-eyebrow {
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 2px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: #B8A07A;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin-bottom: 24px;
  }
  .vellano-research-title {
    font-family: 'Bodoni Moda', serif;
    font-size: clamp(40px, 5vw, 64px);
    line-height: 1.1;
    margin-bottom: 32px;
  }
  .vellano-research-sub {
    font-size: 18px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: #555;
  }
  
  .vellano-research-content {
    max-width: 900px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 60px;
  }
  .vellano-research-block {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 60px;
    align-items: center;
  }
  .vellano-research-block:nth-child(even) {
    direction: rtl;
  }
  .vellano-research-block:nth-child(even) > * {
    direction: ltr;
  }
  .vellano-research-img-wrap {
    border-radius: 16px;
    overflow: hidden;
    position: relative;
  }
  .vellano-research-img-wrap img {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
    display: block;
  }
  .vellano-research-text h3 {
    font-family: 'Bodoni Moda', serif;
    font-size: 32px;
    margin-bottom: 24px;
  }
  .vellano-research-text p {
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: #444;
    margin-bottom: 24px;
  }
  .vellano-research-stat {
    font-family: 'Bodoni Moda', serif;
    font-size: 48px;
    color: #B8A07A;
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }

  @media (max-width: 960px) {
    .vellano-research-block { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 40px; }
    .vellano-research-block:nth-child(even) { direction: ltr; }
  }
{%- endstyle -%}

<div class="vellano-research">
  <div class="vellano-research-header">
    <div class="vellano-research-eyebrow">Clinical Evidence</div>
    <h1 class="vellano-research-title">The hard truth about hard water.</h1>
    <p class="vellano-research-sub">We spent two years engineering the KDF-55 filtration matrix. Here is the clinical breakdown of exactly what it removes from your shower, and how it restores your skin barrier.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="vellano-research-content">
    <div class="vellano-research-block">
      <div class="vellano-research-text">
        <span class="vellano-research-stat">98%</span>
        <h3>Chlorine & Heavy Metal Reduction</h3>
        <p>Municipal water is heavily chlorinated to prevent bacteria, but this same chemical strips the natural oils from your skin and hair. Our kinetic degradation fluxion (KDF) filter utilizes a high-purity copper-zinc formulation to reduce chlorine and heavy metals by up to 98% via an electrochemical oxidation-reduction process.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="vellano-research-img-wrap">
        <img src="{{ 'vellano_water_flow.png' | asset_url }}" alt="Filtration Tech">
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="vellano-research-block">
      <div class="vellano-research-text">
        <span class="vellano-research-stat">pH 5.5</span>
        <h3>Acid Mantle Restoration</h3>
        <p>Hard water is highly alkaline (pH 8+), which disrupts your skin's natural acid mantle (pH 5.5). This causes micro-tears in the lipid barrier, leading to eczema, acne, and trans-epidermal water loss. By neutralizing the water, Vellano allows your skin to naturally regulate its pH balance.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="vellano-research-img-wrap">
        <img src="{{ 'vellano_body_cleanser.png' | asset_url }}" alt="Skin Barrier">
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Vellano Research",
  "presets": [{ "name": "Vellano Research" }]
}
{% endschema %}
